==============================================================================
  APPENDIX S -- THE COMPOSED BOUNDARY AND ITS LIGHTHOUSES
==============================================================================

S.1  THE TWO TERMINI OF A BOUNDARY, AND WHICH ONE IS WRITTEN
     For k odd the termini are the uniform states at Sigma_u = +k and
     Sigma_u = -k, a conjugate pair (Axiom 2.3).  The residual
     terminus is the one at -k: every literal of the boundary
     falsified.  Its conjugate is forced and is never written.

    PASS  the written terminus falsifies every literal of its boundary   105/105   [Sigma_u = -k, the excluded sector]
    PASS  its component-wise opposite stands every literal of its boundary   105/105   [Sigma_u = +k, forced by Axiom 2.2, never written]
    PASS  a terminus bears on exactly the k contents of its own support   105/105   [Axiom 5.1]

S.2  THE THREE RELATIONS ARE EXCLUSIVE AND EXHAUSTIVE
     A boundary stands at its residual terminus, is barred, or is not
     yet determined -- exactly one of the three, on the evidence of
     the contents of its own support.

    PASS  at the residual terminus and barred are never both true   42000/42000   [exclusive]
    PASS  where neither holds, the support is not yet wholly oriented   42000/42000   [exhaustive]
    PASS  a boundary barred at a stratum is barred in every stratum below it   30336/30336   [from Axiom 5.2 and Proposition 14.1]
    PASS  and no address of it stands at that residual terminus   3713/3713

S.3  THE COMPOSED BOUNDARY IS ONE OBJECT
     The family is a function of the asserted boundaries and the
     order of mediation, and of nothing else.

    PASS  the identical family returns under permuted presentation of the boundaries   24/24   [four permutations, both orders, every committed instance]

